import{_ as a,o as t,c as n,a5 as s}from"./chunks/framework.CsGesDJn.js";const u=JSON.parse('{"title":"Workspace chat collaboration","description":"","frontmatter":{},"headers":[],"relativePath":"feature/workspace-chat-collaboration/spec.md","filePath":"feature/workspace-chat-collaboration/spec.md"}'),o={name:"feature/workspace-chat-collaboration/spec.md"};function c(i,e,r,d,l,h){return t(),n("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[s('<h1 id="workspace-chat-collaboration" tabindex="-1">Workspace chat collaboration <a class="header-anchor" href="#workspace-chat-collaboration" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Workspace chat collaboration&quot;">​</a></h1><h2 id="objective-and-user-story" tabindex="-1">Objective and user story <a class="header-anchor" href="#objective-and-user-story" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Objective and user story&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Upgrade <code>/workspaces/:id/chat</code> in the real <code>brandhub-web</code> frontend into an efficient workspace communication surface while preserving authenticated REST/STOMP delivery and BrandHub&#39;s visual identity. Members need to navigate conversations, find messages and recover failed sends without losing the business context.</p><h2 id="acceptance-criteria" tabindex="-1">Acceptance criteria <a class="header-anchor" href="#acceptance-criteria" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Acceptance criteria&quot;">​</a></h2><ol><li>Keep existing MANAGER/CREATOR/CLIENT route and backend access checks. OWNER access does not change.</li><li>Desktop shows a conversation sidebar, message timeline and an optional message details panel. Mobile uses accessible sheets and leaves room for the app&#39;s bottom navigation. Closing a sheet restores keyboard focus to the control that opened it, or to visible chat navigation if that control was removed; transferring between sheets must not steal focus from the newly opened sheet.</li><li>Sidebar lists persisted public/private channels and direct conversations. Selecting a conversation uses its authenticated backend history and access rules.</li><li>Context URLs keep <code>contextType</code> and <code>contextId</code>; selecting a context filters its messages and sends using the same context. Optimistic and failed messages must match the selected context too. Unknown or missing context identifiers never cause an unscoped send.</li><li>Search queries saved channel history by content or sender, with cursor pagination. Pinned-message and thread views use the same channel access checks.</li><li>Messages use readable, left-aligned collaborative rows, clear sender/time/context and accessible copy/details/retry actions. Copy reports success only after the clipboard operation succeeds.</li><li>Failed sends can be retried using the original <code>clientMessageId</code>; another attempt does not duplicate optimistic rows. Send exceptions restore a failed state. Canonical messages are deduplicated by sender plus client ID and sorted by timestamp plus ID.</li><li>Switching workspace or authenticated account cannot retain previous messages, drafts or stale asynchronous results. Incoming events from disposed connections are ignored.</li><li>Reading history or receiving messages while hidden does not automatically mark unseen messages as read; only visible messages in the active view advance read state.</li><li>Loading, empty, history failure with retry, disconnected, sending and failed-send states remain actionable.</li><li>All labels use parallel <code>vi/chat.json</code> and <code>en/chat.json</code> keys under <code>chat.title</code>, <code>chat.loadOlder</code>, <code>chat.connection.*</code>, <code>chat.empty.*</code>, <code>chat.context.*</code>, <code>chat.delivery.*</code>, <code>chat.composer.*</code>, <code>chat.errors.*</code>, <code>chat.ui.*</code>, <code>chat.actions.*</code>, <code>chat.reactions.*</code>, <code>chat.search.*</code>, <code>chat.thread.*</code> and <code>chat.channels.*</code>.</li><li>Use existing semantic theme tokens, typography and shared controls. Verify light/dark, keyboard access and 375/768/1440px widths.</li></ol><h2 id="api-contract" tabindex="-1">API contract <a class="header-anchor" href="#api-contract" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;API contract&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Authenticated channel REST APIs below are the source of truth; STOMP events invalidate channel queries. Preserve legacy general history, read/unread and STOMP contracts without exposing non-general messages. Do not persist server state in localStorage.</p><h2 id="errors-and-edge-cases" tabindex="-1">Errors and edge cases <a class="header-anchor" href="#errors-and-edge-cases" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Errors and edge cases&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Preserve loaded messages on pagination/reconnect failure. Prevent concurrent duplicate history requests. Ignore stale requests after account/workspace changes, including A→B→A transitions. Different senders can legitimately reuse a client message ID. A failed optimistic message may later receive its canonical acknowledgement. Search/context filtering must not strand pagination or silently alter composer context. Render message content as plain text.</p><h2 id="backend-and-collaboration-scope" tabindex="-1">Backend and collaboration scope <a class="header-anchor" href="#backend-and-collaboration-scope" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Backend and collaboration scope&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Deliver persisted PUBLIC/PRIVATE channels, two-person DIRECT conversations, thread replies, reactions, pins, server-side search and channel member/settings management in the real frontend and backend.</p><ul><li>The default <code>general</code> channel reuses the existing workspace history. Existing legacy endpoints must exclude non-general messages, including unread counts and read acknowledgements. No historical messages are deleted.</li><li>MANAGER and CREATOR can create channels; CLIENT can use general, explicitly invited channels and DMs with active workspace members. Public non-general channels are discoverable by internal members; CLIENT must be explicitly invited. Private channels and DMs require explicit membership even for managers.</li><li>Creator or an admitted MANAGER manages a channel. Direct participants are fixed; default general cannot be archived or restricted. Posting can be limited to channel managers; archived channels retain read access and reject all writes except manager restoration/settings.</li><li>Channel creation and DM creation are idempotent through stable request IDs/deterministic DM identity. Concurrent membership changes and settings changes use atomic field updates rather than whole-document replacement.</li><li>Replies reference a root in the same workspace/channel. Nested replies resolve to the original root. Sending retains the existing workspace context validation and sender-scoped idempotency; conflicting reuse of a client ID is rejected.</li><li>Reactions use an allowlisted code and atomic add/remove; pins use idempotent PUT/DELETE. Search is scoped to an admitted channel, uses escaped literal text, is bounded and cursor-paged. Threads and pins use the same membership checks as message history.</li><li>New realtime channel topics are guarded on SUBSCRIBE and every outbound MESSAGE against current workspace plus channel membership. Revoked members stop receiving events. Legacy topics never receive private-channel content.</li><li>Frontend automatically reloads channel settings/history after reconnect, handles removed membership with an accessible error and never continues showing previous private-channel data as the selected channel.</li><li>Mentioning a member is plain-text <code>@name</code> insertion from an authorized directory; this pass does not claim notification delivery, presence or attachment upload. Huddles, video, external integrations, custom role systems and offline push are outside this pass.</li></ul><h3 id="new-contracts" tabindex="-1">New contracts <a class="header-anchor" href="#new-contracts" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;New contracts&quot;">​</a></h3><p><code>/api/v1/workspaces/{workspaceId}/chat/channels</code>: list/create; <code>/{channelId}</code>: update; <code>/{channelId}/members/{userId}</code>: PUT/DELETE; <code>/directory</code>: bounded active-member directory. Channel message APIs live under <code>/{channelId}/messages</code> with <code>before</code>, <code>q</code>, <code>root</code>, and <code>pinned</code> filters. POST creates messages/replies; <code>/{messageId}/reactions/{code}</code> and <code>/{messageId}/pin</code> use PUT/DELETE; <code>/{channelId}/read</code> persists read state. STOMP notifications use <code>/topic/workspaces/{workspaceId}/chat/channels/{channelId}</code> after persistence.</p><h2 id="definition-of-done" tabindex="-1">Definition of done <a class="header-anchor" href="#definition-of-done" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Definition of done&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Frontend typecheck/build and changed-file lint pass; browser fixture checks verify primary workflows, responsive themes and stale-response protection. Report fixture coverage separately from actual multi-user backend testing.</p>',16)])])}const m=a(o,[["render",c]]);export{u as __pageData,m as default};
